[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Direct Sparse Dynamic CPU Qualification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SPARSE-008
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Typed optional AC excitation
STATEMENT: >>>
The C# public request contract shall optionally express independent-source real/imaginary AC amplitudes in SI with the exp(j*omega*t) convention. Omission shall retain the historical serialized request shape. The native boundary shall retain responsibility for semantic validation, and AC override shall not change the nonlinear DC bias excitation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Derived campaign requirement. Implementation: dotnet/Simulator.Client/Requests.cs and generated WireContext metadata. Verification: dotnet/Simulator.Client.Tests/AcContracts.cs omitted-field and real-engine LU/faer analytical response, examples/TypedAc.cs. Native controlled-source families remain broader than the typed SDK; the oracle helper consumes native public JSON explicitly.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SPARSE-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SPARSE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Canonical dynamic sparse combinations
STATEMENT: >>>
Dynamic real and complex assembly shall combine compiler-owned canonical CSC patterns without a dense scan, preserve structural slots through numerical cancellation, and reject dimension, nonfinite scale/value and overflow violations. Retained dense representations remain bounded references and explicit fallbacks rather than evidence of large-circuit scalability.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Derived campaign requirement. Implementation begins with src/sparse.rs::CscPattern::union and CscMatrix::combine_scaled. Verification: tests/sparse_dynamic.rs. Complex assembly/direct AC provider adoption are implemented; checkpoint 384 evidence is in evidence/sparse-384-qualification.md. Wider verification remains incremental.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: PLAN-010
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SPARSE-002
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Complex sparse excitation and provider failure boundaries
STATEMENT: >>>
The solver seam shall accept finite complex excitation vectors and validate every provider response before combining or exposing it. Real-excitation compatibility may superpose two solves; direct complex providers shall support one factorization per requested system. Only explicit Unsupported may trigger a same-provider reference fallback; numerical, resource and transport failures shall propagate.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Derived campaign requirement. Implementation begins with src/linalg.rs and src/solver_contract.rs. Verification: tests/sparse_dynamic.rs legacy vector/shape/finite contracts. Native one-factor complex RHS and AC driver evidence are in tests/sparse_ac.rs, tests/sparse_ac_circuits.rs and checkpoint 384/394 reports.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SPARSE-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SPARSE-003
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Direct sparse AC traversal and independent residuals
STATEMENT: >>>
Linear AC shall assemble G+j*omega*Q from compiler CSC plans and prefer the selected provider's direct complex CSC operation. Explicit Unsupported may use that provider's bounded dense reference path; other errors shall remain failures. Each output shall pass independent sparse componentwise backward-error verification at 1e-10 before publication.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Derived campaign requirement. Implementation: src/ac.rs. Verification: tests/sparse_ac.rs direct-only provider, analytical RC transfer and terminal failure cases. Incremental diode stamps are direct CSC after bounded DC bias. Wider circuit/oracle evidence is recorded in tests/sparse_ac_circuits.rs and evidence/named-ac-*.json; no broad topology qualification is inferred.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SPARSE-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SPARSE-004
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: AC request validation and excitation replacement
STATEMENT: >>>
AC shall validate the complete frequency grid, angular-frequency finiteness, output budget and independent-source overrides before bias/provider work. Excitation shall be assembled from selected complex amplitudes rather than subtracting large nominal terms, reject accumulation overflow, and preserve the raw API nominal-amplitude convention when no override is supplied.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Derived campaign requirement. Implementation: src/ac.rs. Verification: tests/sparse_ac.rs large-nominal voltage/current override regressions across faer and dense LU, and invalid full-grid rejection before nonlinear bias. Iteration 381 first reproduced an incorrect real output with nominal 1e308 and override 1+2j.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SPARSE-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SPARSE-007
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Named independent AC oracle evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
External AC comparisons shall identify the complex signal by name and frequency, select each qualified CPU provider explicitly, disable user initialization scripts, retain immutable input/executable provenance and reject missing/ambiguous/nonfinite reference rows. Tolerances shall reflect actual reference output precision rather than an assumed digit setting. Original qualification decks shall remain distinguished from attributed upstream corpus copies.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Derived campaign requirement. Implementation/verification: scripts/Compare-NamedAcOracle.cs parser negative contracts and actual LU/faer resistor partition, lowpass and original series-RLC comparisons; evidence/named-ac-*.json. Broader selected upstream corpus expansion remains separate.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SPARSE-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SPARSE-006
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Signed dynamic and controlled-source AC conformance
STATEMENT: >>>
Qualified complex CPU paths shall preserve signed inductor branch currents and the declared control/terminal polarities of E/F/G/H source families. Verification shall compare named voltages and branch currents against independent impedance/transfer equations at multiple frequencies and complex source amplitudes.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Derived campaign requirement. Verification: tests/sparse_ac_circuits.rs series RLC including resonance, source-current sign and inductor-current direction, and all four controlled source families. These finite tests do not establish arbitrary topology or conditioning coverage.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SPARSE-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SPARSE-005
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Direct incremental diode conductance
STATEMENT: >>>
At a validated finite bias vector, diode small-signal conductance shall stamp directly into compiler-owned CSC conductance using the analytic terminal derivative and both terminal polarities. Invalid dimensions, nonfinite bias, model-domain violations and stamp overflow shall fail. This capability does not imply a sparse nonlinear DC controller.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Derived campaign requirement. Implementation: src/newton.rs::conductance_at_bias_csc and src/ac.rs. Verification: tests/sparse_ac.rs independent two-diode terminal matrix and malformed/domain cases; existing nonlinear AC regression. SparseAccumulator dimension validation no longer allocates a discarded dense matrix.
<<<
